  "text_input": "Patient presented with yellowish discoloration of eyes for 2 days and giddiness for 2-3 days. History of vomiting (non-projectile, non-bilious). Known case of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (6 years), newly diagnosed Hypertension, and Schizophrenia (15 years). History of left-sided breast carcinoma (2023) post-mastectomy, chemotherapy, and radiation. Current diagnosis includes recurrence of breast lesion with metastasis to lungs, liver, and lymph nodes, surgical site infection, hypothyroidism, hyponatremia (SIADH), and bilateral pleural effusion. Examination showed icterus; vitals stable (BP 120/70, Pulse 78, SpO2 97%). Labs: Hb 12.1, WBC 12100, Platelets 330,000, Bilirubin 7.3, Albumin 3.7, Creatinine 1.0, HbA1c 6.3. Treated with antibiotics (Tufzone), insulin, and supportive care.",
